      "title": "Variable describes investment exposure",
      "narration": "Marcus is comparing permanent policies and notices that several names include the word variable. In variable life, the owner can allocate policy value among the offered investment options in a separate account. Results depend on the selected investments as well as policy funding and charges. The owner bears the specified investment risk and can lose value. This differs from a conventional fixed design's stated crediting guarantees. A separate account is not the same as an indexed interest formula. Ask what is invested, what can change, and which benefit, if any, has a contractual minimum. Similar product names do not establish identical risk.",
