      "title": "Adjustable protection follows the contract’s choices",
      "narration": "Elena's family needs change after a mortgage is repaid. An adjustable life contract can permit changes to the face amount, premium, payment period, or protection plan within its rules. Changing one element can change the others. For example, keeping a lower premium may require less protection or a different protection period under the stated plan. Increasing the insured amount may require evidence of insurability. An ordinary adjustment does not automatically replace the insured with a different person. Some contemporary products use adjustable in a universal-life name. Read the actual mechanics instead of assuming that the word adjustable means unrestricted changes.",
